    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d120">

                <pb facs="0341" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot
                    M–88: Box 2061: CFM Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the Soviet
                            Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                            Ministers</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.F.M. (46) 63</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-09">9 May, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Future Procedure of the
                        Council</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">amendment by the soviet
                        delegation to the proposal of the u.s. delegation (c.f.m. (46) 62)</hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d120-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Para, b) to read as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>1) To call, in accordance with the agreement reached at Moscow, a
                                Peace Conference to meet in Paris on 15th June, <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">on the understanding that agreement will be
                                    reached on the proposed Peace Treaties</hi>, to which draft
                                treaties shall be submitted so that in the final drafting of the
                                treaties the Council shall have the benefit and assistance of the
                                recommendations made by the Peace Conference.</p></quote></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Add the following paragraph to the U.S. draft: <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>c) To instruct the Deputies of the Foreign Ministers to submit not
                                later than 5th June for the approval of the Council of Foreign
                                Ministers, drafts of the proposed Peace Treaties with Italy,
                                Roumania, Bulgaria, Hungary and Finland, in order that these drafts
                                may be presented to a Peace Conference on behalf of the Council of
                                Foreign Ministers. The Council of Foreign Ministers to approve at
                                the <pb facs="0342" n="322" xml:id="pg322"/> same time draft rules
                                of procedure for the Peace Conference and the invitations to the
                                Governments who are to attend it.</p></quote></item>
                </list>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>, 10 May, 1946.<anchor n="95"
                        xml:id="d120-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d120-f1" n="94" xml:id="d120-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg310">p. 310</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d120-f2" n="95" xml:id="d120-f2-content">
                <p>This proposal was originally circulated to the Council of Foreign Ministers
                    during its 14th Meeting, May 9, 6 p.m.; see the United States Delegation Record
                    of that meeting, <ref target="#pg311">p. 311</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
